# An allow-list, not a deny-list.
#
# `COPY . .` in the build stage otherwise pulls in whatever a developer has in
# apps/server — verified: a local `.env` reached /src in the build image and
# `cat /src/.env` printed its contents (#149 review, F5). The final image is
# unaffected (it contains three entries and none of them is this), but the
# build-stage image and the BuildKit cache are readable by anyone with the
# daemon, and WP-C2 puts a Google OAuth client secret in exactly that file.
#
# Inverted deliberately: a deny-list has to be edited every time a new dotfile
# appears, and the failure of forgetting is silent.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!internal/
!migrations/
